{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q423531","formula":"C₁₀H₁₀O₆","hill":"C10H10O6","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":10.0,"O":6.0},"names":{"en":"Chorismic acid","ru":"Хоризмовая кислота"},"descriptions":{"en":"Chorismic acid, more commonly known as its anionic form chorismate, is an important biochemical intermediate in plants and microorganisms. It is a precursor for: The aromatic amino acids phenylalanine, tryptophan, and tyrosine Indole, indole derivatives and tryptophan 2,3-Dihydroxybenzoic acid (DHB) used for enterobactin biosynthesis The plant hormone salicylic acid Many alkaloids and other aromatic metabolites. The folate precursor para-aminobenzoate (pABA) The biosynthesis of vitamin K and folate in plants and microorganisms.","ru":"Хори́змовая кислота, по анионной форме называемая также хоризма́т — органическая двухосновная кислота, является одним из ключевых промежуточных метаболитов шикиматного пути. Хоризмат находится в узловой точке шикиматного пути, за что получил своё название (греч. χωρίζω — раздвоение, вилка)."},"fame":20,"pubchemCid":12039,"mass":226.18,"charge":0,"smiles":"C=C(C(=O)O)O[C@@H]1C=C(C=C[C@H]1O)C(=O)O","inchikey":"WTFXTQVDAKGDEY-HTQZYQBOSA-N","iupac":"(3R,4R)-3-(1-carboxyethenoxy)-4-hydroxycyclohexa-1,5-diene-1-carboxylic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"12039","atoms":26,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.293,"y":1.19,"z":-0.385,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.473,"y":3.092,"z":0.687,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.209,"y":-2.11,"z":0.249,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.08,"y":-2.861,"z":0.615,"el":"O"},{"x":2.065,"y":-0.941,"z":-1.649,"el":"O"},{"x":3.554,"y":-1.509,"z":-0.029,"el":"O"},{"x":0.109,"y":1.294,"z":0.409,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.9,"y":2.229,"z":-0.298,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.381,"y":-0.112,"z":0.638,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.025,"y":1.524,"z":-1.00